# .ctsignore — gitignore-syntax paths that `cts-sync.sh update` will never touch.
# Use for: customized CTS files, pruned CTS files (prevents re-adding them),
# and project-only additions placed under payload directories.
#
# Built during CTS template adoption (2026-06-12). Classification:
#   pruned     = exists in CTS, deliberately deleted in HPW (no frontend here)
#   customized = exists in both, HPW content intentionally differs from CTS

# pruned — HPW has no frontend/UI; re-add from CTS if a UI ever appears
.claude/agents/vue-developer.md
.claude/agents/react-developer.md
.claude/agents/angular-developer.md
.claude/skills/vue-expert/
.claude/skills/react-expert/
.claude/skills/angular-expert/

# customized — HPW's AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md split carries HPW's actual stack
# (NestJS/Nx/ESP32), caveman communication style, embedded-cpp routing,
# HPW's task-file naming rule, and a trimmed Skills/Routing table (no frontend).
# Leading "/" anchors to repo root so nested payload files with the same name
# (e.g. .claude/skills/postgres-best-practices/AGENTS.md) still receive updates.
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md

# customized — HPW settings.json wires Nx/superpowers plugins, ESP32 secrets
# deny-list, and project-specific lint/format hooks; not a generic CTS config.
.claude/settings.json

# customized — HPW rule files use single-quote code samples (matches HPW's
# actual Prettier/ESLint config) and migrations-queue/testing/validation
# examples were rewritten for HPW's stack.
rules/code-style.md
rules/migrations-queue.md
rules/testing.md
rules/validation-authorization.md

# customized — HPW workflow.md is process content re-merged from upstream on
# 2026-07-01 (Foresight gate, Nx Command Execution Policy, sequential quality
# gate, severity floor, CLAUDE_TS_CHANGELOG knowledge routing), then
# frontend-pruned (no impl-team/frontend swimlanes, no Vue/React/Angular rows).
# WARNING: whole-file ignore froze this at mid-June content for ~2 weeks before
# the drift was caught — re-diff against upstream periodically (e.g. every
# /cts-update), don't assume "customized" means "never touch again".
rules/workflow.md

# customized — reviewer/tester had their Vue/React/Angular rows pruned (no
# frontend here); queue-specialist uses HPW's single-quote code style (see
# rules/code-style.md note above). dba.md/qa.md were removed from this list
# once CTS adopted HPW's stale-skill-reference fixes — those files are
# byte-identical, CTS-owned again. tester.md's "Vitest" wording was also
# corrected to "Jest" here (2026-07-01) — see vitest-testing note below.
.claude/agents/reviewer.md
.claude/agents/tester.md
.claude/agents/queue-specialist.md

# customized — HPW is pure Jest (jest.config.ts/.cts in every app/lib,
# jest/ts-jest/@swc/jest deps, zero vitest in package.json). CTS's
# vitest-testing skill body was Vitest-only despite claiming "(or Jest)"
# support; examples rewritten to Jest APIs (jest.fn/jest.mock, no `vitest`
# import) here on 2026-07-01. Candidate to contribute upstream later as a
# wider vitest-or-jest skill, or split into two — not yet. See
# docs/CLAUDE_TS_CHANGELOG.md.
.claude/skills/vitest-testing/
